  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000005946</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preventing human rights violations in the DRC mining sector through promoting multistakeholder dialogue and good security governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mining is an essential economic activity in the DRC but remains a source of insecurity and human rights violations for communities. For over a decade, efforts have been made to achieve standards set by the Organisation for Economic Co-Operation and Development to mitigate and reduce human rights violations related to conflict minerals from eastern DRC. This project seeks to overcome these challenges by building on successful results from prior projects in the DRC that received funding from the Netherlands and other donors through DCAF&#x2019;s Security and Human Rights Implementation Mechanism (SHRIM). Furthermore the project will strengthen human rights training and promote further integration of human rights best practice standards related to the extractives sector for the Congolese National Police in relation to other stakeholders and initiatives. Finally, the project will increase and build leverage to support human rights protections through the VPs processes by identifying the links between human rights, natural resource governance as seen through transparency and anti-corruption lenses, and other due diligence and responsible business initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
